+The OpenStack Compute console type ``spice-direct`` requires that
+SPICE support be compiled into the qemu running the instance. Red Hat
+removed SPICE support from qemu in RHEL9, and Rocky Linux has followed
+suit, so the stock Rocky Linux container images do not support
+``spice-direct`` out of the box.
+
+If you are deploying Kerbside on Rocky Linux, set
+``use_ligenix_qemu = true`` in ``kolla-build.conf`` before building
+``nova-libvirt``. When enabled, the Rocky variant of the
+``nova-libvirt`` image pulls ``qemu-kvm`` and ``spice-server`` from
+the community-maintained
+`ligenix/enterprise-qemu-spice
+<https://copr.fedorainfracloud.org/coprs/ligenix/enterprise-qemu-spice/>`__
+COPR repository, which rebuilds ``qemu-kvm`` with SPICE re-enabled
+for EPEL 9 and EPEL 10. Because this COPR is a third-party rebuild
+without a vendor support contract, it is recommended only for
+proof-of-concept deployments.
+
+The Debian and Ubuntu container images continue to support
+``spice-direct`` without additional configuration.
